Ladybird’s storage.managed is always empty: get() resolves with an
empty object and getBytesInUse() with 0, and every write fails with
“This is a read-only store.” That’s Chromium’s behavior for an extension
without a managed-storage policy, from its ManagedValueStoreCache. Gecko
instead rejects get() with “Managed storage manifest not found” when
there’s no managed-storage manifest, and WebKit’s storage namespace
has no managed area at all.
